  "category": "Class Architecture",
  "scenario": "In a rich-text editor, a Document strictly owns its Page objects (pages cannot exist without the document). Meanwhile, TextBlock and ImageBlock are specialized types of Block.",
  "goal": "Connect Document to Page using Composition, and connect TextBlock and ImageBlock to Block using Generalization.",
  "learningObjective": "Use Composition for strong lifecycle ownership and Generalization for is-a inheritance.",
  "hints": [
    "Composition goes from the whole (Document) to the part (Page) or check the diamond side.",
    "Generalization arrows point from the subclass (TextBlock, ImageBlock) up to the base class (Block)."
  ],
  "solutionExplanation": "Document owns Page via Composition, while TextBlock and ImageBlock inherit from Block via Generalization.",
